 want to work with you  to save our planet and we're pers we're  all committed to finding every  possible avenue of cooperation on  climate  there are many issues on which we don't  all see  eye to eye this isn't one of them  some of those countries said they held  felt this  breath of relief that they were dealing  with the u.s that was  into deep fighting climate change is  that fair looking backwards  you know brett we were very clear it was  america first they have traded that  very clearly for climate change first  that is not good for american security  it won't lead to better outcomes more  prosperity for us here at home  we care deeply about clean air and clean  drinking water we  every republican does that i've ever met  but to think that you're going to do  this by putting these  these rules a top-down command  focused economy that is going to just  have more cylinders more disasters  because we will waste american taxpayers  money you're going to deliver really  good outcomes i think that's just silly  to  hope that that will happen this will  turn out to be enormously expensive  especially for the hard-working men and  women all across america all across  america  but you agree climate change is an issue  that needs to be dealt with  we've all got to do everything we can to  make sure that we are  science-based we're focused on making  sure that we get it right with respect  to  our environment nobody i'm from kansas  our farmers spend more time thinking  about how to keep their rivers and soil  clean and keep the air clean than  anybody else all across the world they  care about this deeply it's important to  them and for their grandchildren  i don't think anybody disputes the fact  that we need to make sure that we have a  focus on keeping our environment safe  i want to turn to a couple of other  issues iran the administration  is signaling uh pulling back sanctions  perhaps as they're trying to get back  into this iran nuclear deal today  the head of centcom said that the  iranians are making  big strides he said quantitative  remarkable improvements in their  ballistic missile force  at the same time your thoughts on all of  this  well to go back into the jcpoa would be  an enormous mistake  and to lift these sanctions sanctions  that we built up over the course of  four years that had put real constraints  on iran's capacity  would be a big mistake you know these  stories right these are terrorists and  they're not going to go declare that  these are not terrorists  i don't see how one can in good faith do  that  they never got a deal that approached  anything that would attack the ballistic  missile program that that general  referred to  we in the other hand denied them over  121 billion dollars in foreign exchange  reserves they had to make  difficult choices about their programs  and america was more secure because of  it we had  with great partners and friends too it  was in america alone the arab states and  israel working alongside of us had iran  more isolated than in any time in  history  afghanistan uh some concerns from the  centcom commander today  also up on capitol hill about possible  taliban attacks as the u.s gets to  pulling out troops he said it's going to  zero  that's something you support and the  president president trump  pushed for but are there concerns in  your mind about how this all happens  yes brett the execution of this has to  be  flawless it has to be done well and the  administration needs to make very clear  that should the taliban make a choice  that's different than the one they've  made for now what's almost the last year  and a half  we haven't had an american soldier  killed there since the agreement that  our administration entered into the  taliban back in the beginning of 2020.  if the taliban changes direction if they  attack an american we need to respond  with the full fire and fury of the  united states of america  we need to make that clear to them they  need to understand and if we do  we'll deter them and if we don't they'll  attack us and we'll have americans put  at risk i  i hope that's not what happens when you  pick a date certain  this far in advance you certainly  increase the risk of that  finally immigration vice president  harris saying she is going to meet  with the leader in guatemala talking  about the northern triangle  countries saying that the potential is  there but it's not going to be  accomplished overnight  thoughts on how they're dealing with  this and focusing on what they say root  causes in the northern triangle  countries  it's funny brett to say that it's not  going to be solved overnight it was  solved before they came into office  we had made enormous progress i spent a  lot of time with the  leaders in honduras el salvador and  guatemala we had an arrangement with  them as well as with the mexican  government that had delivered american  sovereignty we had  secured our border we were finishing out  the building of the wall and we had  diminished  the magnet that drew these people north  that now you can see when you  when you undid it when you undid what  the trump administration had  delivered well it created the magnet  again and now you have a national  security crisis a health crisis  with people coming across not being  tested for the wuhan virus  and a humanitarian crisis of staggering  proportions no they it could actually be  done  almost overnight if they would simply go  back to the policies that the trump  administration had in place  is the bond administration doing  anything good right now  oh yes no they definitely are i was  pleased to see secretary blinken declare  that  it was in fact genocide taking place in  western china  the language that they have used around  the people of hong kong and some of the  sanctions they put in place there  those are all good things i want to  support what this administration is  doing where we can but but  where they're weak and where they're  risking the deterrence that we build up  it's important that the american people  understand that risk very clearly  because it impacts each and every one of  them  former secretary of state mike pompeo  fox news contributor  thank you thank you brett

